  "title": "PCPNDT Act Dismissed by Supreme Court",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court of India ruled that the PCPNDT Act, which was enacted to prohibit the use of prenatal diagnostic techniques for determining the sex of the foetus, is not valid and cannot be used to investigate crimes. The court emphasized that authorities designated under the law must take action in such cases and that police are not meant to be the investigators under this Act.",
